<?nvs
// The child `examples/logging.nvs` watches fail. It throws with nothing
// above it, so the throw leaves the program entirely and ADR 0020 § 1's
// ladder takes over: the operator's handler script runs, charged to the
// engine's own reserve rather than to this script's remaining budget.
//
// There is deliberately no `try` here. A `catch` would make this a program
// that handles its own failure, which is the rung `examples/logging.nvs`
// already shows on its own.
throw new RuntimeError("the child gave up");
